      "message": "`new char[]` default initializes which generally means do nothing. (`new char[]()` would always zero initialize). Are there particular `new` implementations which are zero initializing for default initialization? If so, that would be interesting information to attach to this so that we know which are the offenders. (`malloc` is also free to zero initialize and it would also be interesting to know if any `malloc`s do that as well. If someone wrote their global `new` to zero, there isn\u0027t anything preventing `malloc` from doing the same.)",
